course: dictionary
lesson: 9111
title: Your nose and smell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Smell can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to smell means to notice something with your nose: «You smell cookies baking from the other room.» As a noun, a smell is the thing you notice: «a smell of smoke».
explain: Your nose works like a message system. Tiny bits of a thing float through the air, up your nose, and land on smell cells. Those cells send a signal to your brain, which says «cookies!». This is why smell is one of the five senses.
explain: Smell can warn you. A smell of smoke, gas or burning means danger, so get out and tell an adult. Food with a bad smell may be spoiled, so do not eat it.
fact: Smell means to notice something with your nose.
fact: Smell is one of the five senses, and your nose sends signals to your brain.
fact: «Rotten eggs smell» because tiny bacteria break down parts of the egg and give off a gas.
fact: Dogs smell far better than people do.
fact: A smell of smoke, gas or burning means danger: get out and tell an adult.
exercise: «You smell cookies baking from the other room.» What does smell mean here? | To feel very hungry | To cook food | *To notice something with your nose | To give off a bad smell
exercise: Which of the five senses uses your nose? | *Smell | Sight | Hearing
exercise: You notice «a smell of smoke» in your house. What should you do? | Keep cooking and ignore it | Hide the smell under a blanket | Open the window and sniff again to be sure | *Get out and tell an adult
test: «The flowers smell sweet.» What does smell mean in this sentence? | To cook food | *To give off a smell | To notice something with your nose | To feel soft
test: Toad notices «the smell of hot cabbage». What is a smell? | *What you notice with your nose | A loud noise | The name of a food | A thing you can touch
exam: Which sentence uses smell as a noun, meaning the thing you notice with your nose? | «They smell the sea.» | *«She noticed a smell of toast.» | «Your socks smell!» | «The dog will smell the bone.»
